# Item views come from the catalog

`ItemViewId` is a separate enum from socket type (`ShipModuleType`). Every pickup visual is a prefab registered in `ItemViewCatalog`. Sockets spawn that prefab at an install point. Do not leave a pre-placed mesh inside the socket.

The same view prefab is instanced on the world item. If the item mesh is not that catalog prefab, the prefab is assembled wrong — say so and fix it.

```csharp
// BAD — view baked into the socket
[SerializeField] private GameObject _installedView;

// GOOD — catalog + spawn at a per-view point
[SerializeField] private Transform _defaultInstallPoint;
[SerializeField] private ItemViewInstallPoint[] _viewInstallPoints;
_catalog.TryGetPrefab(item.View, out GameObject prefab);
Instantiate(prefab, ResolveInstallPoint(item.View));
```

- Add a new look: new `ItemViewId`, view prefab, catalog entry, same prefab as child of the item, optional `ItemViewInstallPoint` on sockets that attach it differently
- Sockets accept a `ShipModuleType`; they do not store view prefabs
